  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072619/assets/6c5ce500d937822081d819e2c02f5fabece926498dd196e65d64dbdaa1dcb0bc.png)\n\nConsider the RC circuit shown above. Given that the charge $q(t)$ of the capacitor at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nq(t)=A{e}^{-4t}+\\frac{P}{125}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)+\\frac{Q}{125}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $P,$ and $Q$ are constants, find the value of $P+Q.$\n\n*Hint: The voltage drop ${V}_{C}$ across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C},$ where $C$ is the capacitance measured in Farads.*",
